From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:33:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: gts3lwifi: Bluetooth holds the Rome 3.3 V
 rail

The QCA6174 is powered from vreg_rome_3p3, which the PCIe host also
switches through WLAN_EN. In system suspend pcie-qcom powers the
endpoint off, which took Bluetooth down too: it came back in its ROM
state, missed the in-band wake, and its recovery kept the following
suspends from completing. Stock gives Bluetooth the same rail as its
qca,bt-vdd-pa-supply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
index b4e723b31..9cc148eaf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
@@ -1346,6 +1346,11 @@ bluetooth {
 		compatible = "qcom,qca6174-bt";
 		enable-gpios = <&pm8994_gpios 19 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		clocks = <&rome_sleep_clk>;
+		/*
+		 * Rome's 3.3 V rail, which also feeds WLAN_EN: the PCIe host
+		 * drops its vote in suspend (stock: qca,bt-vdd-pa-supply).
+		 */
+		vddpa-supply = <&vreg_rome_3p3>;
 	};
 };
 
